From c66d301a02b7d7753a5c0adcf3aa5046d702221c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:10:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: bug 13b: free cells deep through records with a
 stack of pending releases

0013 frees a chain of cells in a loop, but drop_and_free still released
the other chain members about to be freed recursively. A value deep along
a member that is not the one the loop follows (a tree deep along its left
child whose right children are fresh nodes; a rose tree whose child lists
hold the deep tree in their head and a fresh node in their tail) still took
a stack frame per level and overflowed (lean2rr: 10^6 levels at an 8 MB
stack, where native Lean frees iteratively).

The drop glue now uses one stack of pending releases per thread, as Lean's
lean_del does with its to-do list. Inside drop glue a member that is a
plain shared record box is, when its count is 1, deferred with its type's
drop_and_free (new op reussir.rc.defer_release, lowered to the runtime's
__reussir_drop_defer); otherwise decremented. drop_in_place, the glue
entry, drains the stack before returning (__reussir_drop_drain; a drain
started while one runs returns at once, so the outermost one runs all the
work). drop_and_free, which only runs from a drain, releases a cell's
members (deferring its record boxes) but the last record box, frees the
cell, and releases that box by a tail call when its count is 1, so a chain
is still a loop. Draining dtors and drop_and_free do not claim nocallback.
drop_and_free is now named drop_and_free_in_drain, as its contract changed
(it must run inside a drain), so it cannot merge, as a linkonce_odr
definition, with one from an rrc without the stack.

Like Lean's list, the stack takes no memory per pending cell (freeing a
list whose elements are boxes keeps every element pending until the spine
is freed): consecutive deferred cells form one entry, linked through the
cells themselves. A deferred cell's count is known to be 1, so 48 bits of
its header word (the count, and the upper half of the word after it,
padding or a fused tag below 2^16, which is kept) hold the offset to the
previous cell (40 bits, in 8-byte units) and that cell's release function
(the same as this cell's, or an index in a small per-thread table emptied
with the stack). The compiler defers such boxes through
__reussir_drop_defer_wide; a box without that header room is deferred
unlinked (__reussir_drop_defer), and a box of a record with no managed
members is freed at once, not deferred (it cannot recurse and has no
effect to order). The stack shrinks back after a large drain.

The runtime also lets a host share the stack (active, depth, defer_step,
run_step), so that a host's own iterative frees and the glue release
everything in one order.
